=== NOTES ===
- Engine validates inputs and throws RangeError with stable codes ALGO_INPUT_INVALID, LADDER_INPUT_INVALID, THRESHOLD_INVALID, BRACKETS_INVALID; results never contain NaN or Infinity.
- traceAlgorithm keeps the full correct sorted/foundIndex result even when frames are cut at maxFrames (default 400); only frames are sliced and truncated is set true.
- Engine-level input validation is generic (finite integers) rather than the gen limits (4..10 items, 0..99); ALG-03 range/shape rules stay in the validator.
- Binary search uses mid = floor((lo+hi)/2); narrow frames carry the new inclusive range, or null when that half is empty; merge split/merge ranges are inclusive [lo, hi-1].
- ladderDirection for equal from/to uses (to > from) === increasing, so equal returns less when increasing and more otherwise; cases in the spec always have from != to.
- fractionWords returns hyphen, space, and n/d variants for the five named fractions (3/4 includes both fourths and quarters wording) and plain n/d otherwise.
- parseTableNumber is strict: optional sign, optional one $, thousands commas only in correct groups, optional decimal, optional trailing %; percent returns the face number (37% -> 37); unicode minus variants normalized; -0 normalized to 0; everything else returns null.
- progressiveTax taxes [over[i], over[i+1]) slices at rate[i] percent with the last bracket open-ended to income; income 0 yields total 0 with no parts.
- No deviations from section 2 signatures; index.ts only re-exports the four engine modules.
